# Copy, cut, paste via the private clipboard (the user's clipboard is untouched).
open "$DIR/chapter.md"
click_index 5 2
key C cmd
expect clipboard "fog"
wait 30
click_index 0
key V cmd
expect text "fogThe fog came in off the fjord the way it always did in late October: quietly, completely, and without asking. Zoë Ångström stood at the top of the lighthouse stairs with a lantern in one hand and her grandmother’s letter in the other.\n\n“You’re late,” said Dvořák.\n"
key Z cmd
expect text "The fog came in off the fjord the way it always did in late October: quietly, completely, and without asking. Zoë Ångström stood at the top of the lighthouse stairs with a lantern in one hand and her grandmother’s letter in the other.\n\n“You’re late,” said Dvořák.\n"
wait 30
click_index 5 2
key X cmd
expect clipboard "fog"
expect text "The  came in off the fjord the way it always did in late October: quietly, completely, and without asking. Zoë Ångström stood at the top of the lighthouse stairs with a lantern in one hand and her grandmother’s letter in the other.\n\n“You’re late,” said Dvořák.\n"
key Z cmd
expect text "The fog came in off the fjord the way it always did in late October: quietly, completely, and without asking. Zoë Ångström stood at the top of the lighthouse stairs with a lantern in one hand and her grandmother’s letter in the other.\n\n“You’re late,” said Dvořák.\n"
# Pasted CRLF is normalised and control characters are dropped.
clipboard "one\r\ntwo\u{1}"
key END cmd
key V cmd
expect text "The fog came in off the fjord the way it always did in late October: quietly, completely, and without asking. Zoë Ångström stood at the top of the lighthouse stairs with a lantern in one hand and her grandmother’s letter in the other.\n\n“You’re late,” said Dvořák.\none\ntwo"
key A cmd
key C cmd
expect clipboard "The fog came in off the fjord the way it always did in late October: quietly, completely, and without asking. Zoë Ångström stood at the top of the lighthouse stairs with a lantern in one hand and her grandmother’s letter in the other.\n\n“You’re late,” said Dvořák.\none\ntwo"
